# Cloudflare Pages headers. Long-cache the immutable LaTeX/Typst engine + bundled TeX assets: these
# are content-stable static files served from public/ (which Vite/Pages do NOT content-hash), so they
# need an explicit cache rule to avoid re-downloading hundreds of MB of WASM on every visit.
#
# IMPORTANT — this file intentionally sets NO Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy / Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy.
# The LaTeX engine (texlyre-busytex) and Typst run on plain postMessage, not SharedArrayBuffer, so
# cross-origin isolation is NOT required — and adding COOP/COEP under `require-corp` would break the
# Supabase signed-image loading (those <img> from *.supabase.co carry no CORP header). See plan §0.

/assets/busytex/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/tex/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/wasm/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
